Simplest: On mobile (≤880), make status panel a compact horizontal summary and place it *after* the topbar but *before* story, with the ship log details collapsed. That is likely the original order. To prevent it taking too much space, hide the "Mission Readout" heading and the log by default on mobile, show stat grid 6 columns or 3x2. Actually 6 columns at 370px width: each 55px, labels like "Supplies" at 0.6rem may fit. Values. Height ~60px. Good. Ship log details can remain but collapsed by default? The `open` attribute is in HTML. CSS can't close details. We could use JS to remove `open` on mobile only, but not needed if status panel has a details after stat grid; if open it adds log list height. We can hide log entirely on mobile? The full log is in menu. Better CSS `@media max-width 880 { .fleet-box { display:none } .status-panel h2 { display:none } .status-panel .stat-grid { margin:0 } }`. Stats strip only. The ship log is accessible in menu. That's clean. Reorder status before story on mobile:
