await (async (page) => { await page.evaluate(async () => { window.eval('state.started=false'); localStorage.clear(); const regs = await navigator.serviceWorker.getRegistrations(); await Promise.all(regs.map(r => r.unregister())); const keys = await caches.keys(); await Promise.all(keys.map(k => caches.delete(k))); }); await page.reload(); await page.waitForTimeout(400); return {title:await page.locator('#scene h2').innerText(), statsVisible:await page.locator('#stats').isVisible(), feature:await page.locator('.feature-chip span').first().innerText(), sw:await page.evaluate(async()=> (await navigator.serviceWorker.getRegistrations()).length )}; })(page);
```

Stats visible on title; hidden? No CSS hides stats only on mobile maybe; title state on mobile still shows stats strip above story title, with default stats. Hmm on title screen, the stats strip (24 crew, etc.) appears above the title card on mobile (order 1). Is that desirable? On title, you shouldn't show mission stats for a game not started. The desktop title shows default stats in left panel; that's a bit odd. Should hide the status panel on title entirely for both desktop/mobile. On title screen, mission readout isn't relevant (though record shown in title side panel). Better hide status panel when `body[data-screen="title"]`:
```
body[data-screen="title"] .status-panel { display:none; }
body[data-screen="title"] .game-shell { display:block? }
```
On desktop, game-shell grid with only story panel would occupy second column if status hidden? Grid auto places story in column 1 (min 260) and leaves empty column? Since grid-template-columns 260px 1fr, story panel is first child after hidden? Display:none removes it, story becomes first grid item in 260px column—bad. Better when title:
```
body[data-screen="title"] .game-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; display:block; }
body[data-screen="title"] .status-panel { display:none; }
```
For mobile flex, `display:block` okay but maybe `display:flex` inherited; specificity body... .game-shell beats media? It has higher specificity. Set `grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr)` and `display:grid`? On mobile `.game-shell` display flex; body[data-screen] rule display grid overrides, fine, one column. Use:
```
body[data-screen="title"] .game-shell { display:block; min-height:0; }
